CI tcc lane: test_misc (and test_slice21) CRASH at startup under tcc 0.9.27.

SYMPTOM (first ever runs of build:debian-tcc, poseidon docker runner, and
reproduced locally in registry.gitlab.com/bocl/bocl/ci/debian-tcc:latest):
  # Testing test_misc
  ./test_misc: : Unknown error 86781117
  status=175
The binary BUILDS (tcc compiles + links everything, only might-return-no-value
warnings) but exits abnormally at startup; test_slice21 likewise.  The other
~40 suites pass under tcc.

Not yet root-caused: could be a tcc 0.9.27 miscompilation (the lane's whole
purpose is catching gcc/clang-isms), a too-large/too-new construct in these
two suites' code (big adjacent string literals? setjmp-heavy paths?), or a
genuine bocl portability bug tcc exposes.  NOTE the lane had NEVER run before
the poseidon runners took the pipeline, so this is not necessarily a
regression — bisect by (a) building at older tags in the tcc image, and
(b) minimising test_misc (link an empty main against libbocl-as-built-by-tcc
first: the 'Unknown error' at exec smells like a loader/symbol problem with
the tcc-built shared lib rather than test code).

Repro:
  docker run --rm -v <checkout>:/w -w /w \
    registry.gitlab.com/bocl/bocl/ci/debian-tcc:latest sh -c 'sh ci/build.sh'

Until fixed, build:debian-tcc is allow_failure (v1.8.42): the lane reports
compiler-matrix status without blocking the deliverable pipeline (same policy
as freebsd/macos).
